<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nominoe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 851</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nominoe was the first ruler of a united Brittany, a Breton noble and count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vannes">Vannes</a> whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> appointed as his representative there in 831. After Louis's death he broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, defeated him at Ballon in 845 and made Brittany independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a>. He died in 851 while campaigning against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> and was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a> later honoured him as father of their nation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nominoe.jpg" alt="Nominoe" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Tenniel / Joseph Swain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nom%C3%A9no%C3%AB_(Tenniel).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
